  "_shapes": "Real speedball bunkers, and only simple shapes: CAN (upright tube), DORITO (triangle to poke over), SNAKE (long low tube you play prone behind), BRICK (rectangle lying down), STANDUP (rectangle upright), BALL (the big round one). A 'centreBall' bunker with a domed top on rounded corners used to sit at the centre and read as a turret from across the field; there are no towers on a paintball field. Match/Inflatables.luau builds each as welded PVC -- bulged panels, darker seam rings, webbing anchor straps -- and gives it one invisible collision box matching the oriented box declared here, so player collision, bot line-of-sight and projectile blocking are all the same shape.",
  "_mirror": "Pieces with mirrorZ:true are duplicated with Z negated, giving the symmetric field. Pieces with mirrorX:true are duplicated with X negated.",
